WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.980
Marvel recently dropped a bombshell when it
announced that the Blade franchise is getting

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
a reboot, and that Oscar-winning actor Mahershala
Ali is taking the reins as the new Eric Brooks.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.840
In the few days following that news, it seemed
everyone had something to say about the reboot.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.060
There were plenty of tweets expressing excitement
over Ali's casting, and then there were those

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:24.300
that weren't so thrilled - including one promise
to "riot" if original Blade actor Wesley Snipes

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.060
wasn't involved with the new movie.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.260
And now, Snipes has finally broken his silence
on the Blade reboot and Ali stepping into

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:30.780
his shoes.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.360
It turns out, Snipes is totally cool with
the whole thing, and thinks you should be

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:34.860
too.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.620
"No, no, no I ain't pissed off."

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.880
ComicBook.com obtained a statement from Snipes
in which he affirms that there are no hard

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.820
feelings toward Ali and he's not disappointed
over Marvel choosing to reboot Blade without

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.020
him - just complete understanding.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:55.040
In his statement, Snipes even used two Arabic
phrases - "salaam," meaning "peace," and "inshallah,"

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.280
meaning "if God wills".

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:04.280
This is extra special, since Ali is Muslim
and Snipes practiced Islam from 1978 to 1988,

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.580
according to The Hollowverse.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.080
Snipes said, in part,

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.200
"To all the DAYWALKERS losing their minds
right now, chillaaxx.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.780
Although the news comes as a surprise, it's
ALL GOOD.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.700
Such is the 'business' of 'entertainment!'

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.200
Much peace to the MCU crew – always a fan.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.480
Honor and respect to the grandmaster Stan
[Lee].

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.970
Congratulations and Salaam to Mahershala Ali,
a beautiful and talented artist whose expressions

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:28.500
I look forward to experiencing for many years
to come.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.680
Inshallah, we will someday work together.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.960
Most importantly to my loyal fans, the incredible
outpouring of love is overwhelming.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.220
I am grateful for the never-ending support."

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:41.490
It's always tricky business when a studio
decides to reimagine a property with a brand-new

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.170
face at the forefront - and when it comes
to Blade, a movie that changed the superhero

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.890
genre forever and has continued to influence
comic book adaptations to this day, there

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.640
was an even bigger risk for vicious attacks
from those opposed to the entire idea.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.340
"Why can't you just be nice?"

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.640
'Cause the world isn't nice."

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:07.280
While the Blade reboot has already garnered
some backlash, it hasn't been as bad as it

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.140
could have been, considering the circumstances.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.460
According to Vice, Snipes has long wanted
to play the vampire-hunting Daywalker again.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.940
This is a classy response from Snipes.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.980
There's certainly a chance that he feels a
bit upset about Ali taking over the franchise

00:02:19.989 --> 00:02:24.269
and Marvel not yet extending an offer to appear
in the reboot in some capacity, but Snipes

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:25.880
seems genuine in his response.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.840
He's right in saying that reboots are just
part of the entertainment business - especially

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.409
these days, when studios are constantly looking
to refresh properties for new generations

00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:37.660
and draw in old fans with the irresistible
pull of nostalgia.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.650
It was really only a matter of time before
Marvel looked to what's largely considered

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:46.980
the grandfather of superhero movies for a
refresh as the studio maps out its post-Infinity

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:47.940
Saga plans.

00:02:48.109 --> 00:02:52.400
The Blade franchise rests in capable hands
with Ali, and Snipes can understand that.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.560
His mention that he hopes to one day work
with Ali could spark talk of a potential Blade

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.889
reboot sequel in which Snipes does actually
have a role, but considering the first flick

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:04.980
is currently without a release date, writer,
or director, those conversations probably

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.640
wouldn't amount to anything substantial for
quite some time.

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:11.860
With Snipes having now broken his silence
about the Blade reboot, fans can now rest

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:16.319
easy knowing the only blood that will be spilt
is the blood that will go flying in the film

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:16.820
itself.

